1
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:05,879
If your family needed to make a funeral claim

2
00:00:05,679 --> 00:00:06,957
who would they call?

3
00:00:07,257 --> 00:00:10,805
Would they know where to find the policy, who is covered

4
00:00:10,605 --> 00:00:12,039
and what to do first?

5
00:00:12,339 --> 00:00:16,995
Those are practical questions a family can answer while there is still time to plan.

6
00:00:17,295 --> 00:00:18,492
This is Ayanda.

7
00:00:18,292 --> 00:00:22,013
Tonight, she and her mother are at the kitchen table

8
00:00:21,813 --> 00:00:27,194
saving an important number and putting the family's documents into one folder.

9
00:00:28,494 --> 00:00:31,225
This is where the EquiGrowth story begins.

10
00:00:31,525 --> 00:00:32,569
In this film

11
00:00:32,369 --> 00:00:36,787
we'll follow Ayanda as she explores funeral cover for her family

12
00:00:36,587 --> 00:00:39,124
and Thandi, an appointed consultant

13
00:00:38,924 --> 00:00:44,251
as she explains how EquiGrowth works and looks after the policies she services.

14
00:00:45,551 --> 00:00:49,906
EquiGrowth is the public brand of MyEquiGrowth (Pty) Ltd.

15
00:00:50,206 --> 00:00:54,554
It was established in 2024 as a Black empowerment company

16
00:00:54,354 --> 00:00:57,486
built on relationships: with its clients

17
00:00:57,286 --> 00:01:01,205
with its business partners, and within its own team.

18
00:01:01,505 --> 00:01:08,153
Its founders describe a wider ambition to build wealth-building solutions with partners over time.

19
00:01:07,953 --> 00:01:12,167
That broader story is separate from the product in this film.

20
00:01:11,967 --> 00:01:15,655
Today, we are talking about one thing: funeral cover

21
00:01:15,455 --> 00:01:17,629
and the people who service it.

22
00:01:17,929 --> 00:01:21,629
EquiGrowth describes its strengths as five pillars.

23
00:01:21,429 --> 00:01:23,138
Rather than list them

24
00:01:22,938 --> 00:01:26,775
let's watch them at work in an ordinary conversation.

25
00:01:28,075 --> 00:01:29,109
Stewardship.

26
00:01:28,909 --> 00:01:33,278
When Ayanda asks a question Thandi can't answer on the spot

27
00:01:33,078 --> 00:01:36,404
Thandi takes ownership of it, writes it down

28
00:01:36,204 --> 00:01:38,003
and follows it through.

29
00:01:38,303 --> 00:01:39,228
Integrity.

30
00:01:39,028 --> 00:01:42,422
Before she tells Ayanda who can be included

31
00:01:42,222 --> 00:01:46,197
Thandi checks the policy detail instead of guessing.

32
00:01:46,497 --> 00:01:47,838
A cohesive team.

33
00:01:47,638 --> 00:01:52,047
A colleague helps her find the right version of a document

34
00:01:51,847 --> 00:01:54,330
so Ayanda gets one clear answer.

35
00:01:54,630 --> 00:01:56,487
Continuous improvement.

36
00:01:56,287 --> 00:02:00,451
When customers say part of an explanation is confusing

37
00:02:00,251 --> 00:02:04,847
the team rewrites it, and the next family has an easier time.

38
00:02:05,147 --> 00:02:07,601
And quality service and support.

39
00:02:07,401 --> 00:02:10,770
Ayanda leaves with her paperwork in her hand

40
00:02:10,570 --> 00:02:13,446
and she knows exactly whom to contact.

41
00:02:14,746 --> 00:02:17,654
Now, an important question for any family:

42
00:02:17,454 --> 00:02:20,040
who actually stands behind the cover?

43
00:02:20,340 --> 00:02:23,543
The name Ayanda sees is EquiGrowth.

44
00:02:23,343 --> 00:02:28,346
Behind the brand is the company, MyEquiGrowth (Pty) Ltd.

45
00:02:28,646 --> 00:02:34,478
MyEquiGrowth is a juristic representative of Sibiya Brokers

46
00:02:34,278 --> 00:02:38,326
a financial services provider, FSP 46798.

47
00:02:38,626 --> 00:02:43,629
That means the financial services are provided under Sibiya Brokers' authorisation.

48
00:02:43,929 --> 00:02:49,415
Anyone can check a financial services provider's status on the FSCA's public register.

49
00:02:49,715 --> 00:02:54,085
EquiGrowth's partnership information also names the Mthembe Group

50
00:02:53,885 --> 00:02:56,359
and it names RMA as the underwriter.

51
00:02:56,659 --> 00:03:00,458
In everyday language, the underwriter is the insurer.

52
00:03:00,258 --> 00:03:02,903
It carries the risk that is covered

53
00:03:02,703 --> 00:03:05,484
under the terms written in the policy.

54
00:03:05,784 --> 00:03:10,397
So for Ayanda, these names answer three different questions.

55
00:03:10,197 --> 00:03:12,015
Who am I dealing with?

56
00:03:11,815 --> 00:03:17,090
Under whose financial services authorisation is the service provided?

57
00:03:16,890 --> 00:03:21,871
And which insurer stands behind the cover described in my policy?

58
00:03:22,171 --> 00:03:25,200
Each answer belongs in her policy documents

59
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:27,450
so she never has to rely on memory.

60
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:32,748
EquiGrowth's revised offer is simple to describe:

61
00:03:32,548 --> 00:03:36,081
one funeral cover package, at R430 a month.

62
00:03:36,381 --> 00:03:40,030
Every family on the package pays the same R430.

63
00:03:39,830 --> 00:03:44,946
The consultant's level makes no difference to the customer's price.

64
00:03:46,246 --> 00:03:51,309
Thandi takes Ayanda through the questions a family should ask about any funeral policy.

65
00:03:51,609 --> 00:03:54,654
First: who can be included on my policy?

66
00:03:54,454 --> 00:03:57,002
Thandi opens the policy schedule

67
00:03:56,802 --> 00:04:00,631
and they check the list of insured people together.

68
00:04:00,931 --> 00:04:04,463
Second: how much cover applies to each person?

69
00:04:04,263 --> 00:04:08,448
The schedule sets out the amount for each insured life.

70
00:04:08,248 --> 00:04:10,911
Thandi reads it from the document

71
00:04:10,711 --> 00:04:13,592
not from memory or an older brochure.

72
00:04:13,892 --> 00:04:16,140
Third: when does cover start

73
00:04:15,940 --> 00:04:19,388
and which waiting periods or exclusions apply?

74
00:04:19,188 --> 00:04:21,507
Those are in the policy terms

75
00:04:21,307 --> 00:04:25,179
and Thandi marks them so Ayanda can find them again.

76
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:28,364
And fourth: what should the family keep

77
00:04:28,164 --> 00:04:30,915
and whom should they contact to claim?

78
00:04:30,715 --> 00:04:33,868
The claims contact goes into Ayanda's phone

79
00:04:33,668 --> 00:04:36,418
and the schedule goes into the folder.

80
00:04:36,718 --> 00:04:41,394
If an answer isn't clear on paper, the right response is:

81
00:04:41,194 --> 00:04:43,829
let me confirm that in writing.

82
00:04:43,629 --> 00:04:44,928
Never a guess.

83
00:04:45,228 --> 00:04:48,924
Ayanda writes down one thing she wants confirmed

84
00:04:48,724 --> 00:04:51,350
and Thandi notes it for follow-up.

85
00:04:51,150 --> 00:04:54,132
That is stewardship again, in practice.

86
00:04:55,432 --> 00:04:56,873
Alongside the cover

87
00:04:56,673 --> 00:05:01,217
EquiGrowth's presentation describes member benefits for everyday life.

88
00:05:01,517 --> 00:05:04,783
These include grocery and pharmacy coupons

89
00:05:04,583 --> 00:05:07,421
selected retail and airtime vouchers

90
00:05:07,221 --> 00:05:09,631
travel and lifestyle discounts

91
00:05:09,431 --> 00:05:11,770
and a home assistance service.

92
00:05:12,070 --> 00:05:15,964
Thandi shows Ayanda which of these are attached to her package

93
00:05:15,764 --> 00:05:17,958
according to her benefit schedule.

94
00:05:19,258 --> 00:05:20,655
Before she shops

95
00:05:20,455 --> 00:05:25,375
Ayanda checks that her grocery voucher is eligible and still valid.

96
00:05:25,175 --> 00:05:27,417
Then she uses it at the till.

97
00:05:28,717 --> 00:05:30,545
When a pipe bursts at home

98
00:05:30,345 --> 00:05:32,656
she calls the home assistance line

99
00:05:32,456 --> 00:05:36,395
and the service arranges a qualified professional to come out.

100
00:05:36,695 --> 00:05:40,666
Arranging help is not the same as paying the whole bill.

101
00:05:40,466 --> 00:05:44,302
What the service covers, and what Ayanda pays herself

102
00:05:44,102 --> 00:05:46,457
is set out in the benefit terms.

103
00:05:47,757 --> 00:05:51,389
The presentation also mentions a cashback benefit.

104
00:05:51,189 --> 00:05:53,243
The amount, what qualifies

105
00:05:53,043 --> 00:05:58,597
and when it pays are details Ayanda should see in writing for her own package.

106
00:05:58,897 --> 00:06:02,152
So here is the distinction worth remembering.

107
00:06:01,952 --> 00:06:07,041
The family receives the policy and the member benefits that apply to it.

108
00:06:06,841 --> 00:06:10,979
Consultant compensation is earned through a separate role.

109
00:06:11,279 --> 00:06:13,989
Customers never need to recruit anyone

110
00:06:13,789 --> 00:06:15,469
or become a consultant

111
00:06:15,269 --> 00:06:17,914
to keep their cover or their benefits.

112
00:06:19,214 --> 00:06:22,751
Joining starts at the website: myequigrowth.

113
00:06:22,551 --> 00:06:23,055
com.

114
00:06:23,355 --> 00:06:27,449
Ayanda selects sign up and enters her own details: her name

115
00:06:27,249 --> 00:06:30,500
her active mobile number and her email address.

116
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:33,910
She checks every field before she submits.

117
00:06:33,710 --> 00:06:36,059
Then she completes her profile

118
00:06:35,859 --> 00:06:39,593
including her bank details for the monthly payment.

119
00:06:39,893 --> 00:06:42,322
If anything on the form is unclear

120
00:06:42,122 --> 00:06:45,315
the EquiGrowth office can help her complete it.

121
00:06:45,615 --> 00:06:50,450
Ayanda saves her documents and contact details in the family folder.

122
00:06:50,250 --> 00:06:52,903
Her story as a customer is complete

123
00:06:52,703 --> 00:06:55,970
whether or not she ever becomes a consultant.

124
00:06:57,270 --> 00:07:00,037
Now, let's spend some time with Thandi.

125
00:07:00,337 --> 00:07:02,869
Thandi is an appointed consultant.

126
00:07:02,669 --> 00:07:05,750
Before she could explain or arrange cover

127
00:07:05,550 --> 00:07:10,620
the financial services provider confirmed what she is authorised to do.

128
00:07:10,920 --> 00:07:14,795
A person can apply for appointment without buying the package

129
00:07:14,595 --> 00:07:16,811
and nobody pays to unlock a level.

130
00:07:17,111 --> 00:07:19,973
Her appointment comes with responsibilities:

131
00:07:19,773 --> 00:07:21,969
explaining the policy accurately

132
00:07:21,769 --> 00:07:23,965
servicing the families she signs

133
00:07:23,765 --> 00:07:26,083
and keeping their records in order.

134
00:07:27,383 --> 00:07:33,149
EquiGrowth's revised system gives appointed consultants 13 portfolio milestones.

135
00:07:32,949 --> 00:07:36,141
A consultant progresses through the active

136
00:07:35,941 --> 00:07:39,481
paid policies she personally sells and services.

137
00:07:39,781 --> 00:07:42,676
Here is how the money works.

138
00:07:42,476 --> 00:07:43,735
One policy.

139
00:07:43,535 --> 00:07:46,720
One qualifying monthly payment.

140
00:07:46,520 --> 00:07:50,475
R80 allocated to the compensation pool.

141
00:07:50,775 --> 00:07:53,524
A family on one policy counts once.

142
00:07:53,324 --> 00:07:57,094
If Ayanda's policy covers several family members

143
00:07:56,894 --> 00:08:00,372
it is still one policy in Thandi's portfolio.

144
00:08:00,672 --> 00:08:04,356
For every qualifying active policy paid that month

145
00:08:04,156 --> 00:08:07,226
R80 is allocated to the compensation pool.

146
00:08:07,026 --> 00:08:12,281
The consultant's individual payment follows the agreed remuneration terms.

147
00:08:13,581 --> 00:08:15,962
These are the 13 milestones.

148
00:08:16,262 --> 00:08:20,976
At level 1, Thandi services 2 paid policies.

149
00:08:20,776 --> 00:08:25,183
2 times R80 gives a monthly pool of R160.

150
00:08:25,483 --> 00:08:30,053
At level 2, 4 policies: R320.

151
00:08:29,853 --> 00:08:34,422
At level 3, 8 policies: R640.

152
00:08:34,722 --> 00:08:39,270
Each milestone doubles the number of policies.

153
00:08:39,070 --> 00:08:43,241
Levels 4 to 8 run from 16 policies to 256.

154
00:08:43,541 --> 00:08:49,824
Levels 9 to 13 run from 512 policies up to 8, 192.

155
00:08:50,124 --> 00:08:52,754
Three things matter when you read this chart.

156
00:08:53,054 --> 00:08:57,356
First, the milestones are snapshots of portfolio size.

157
00:08:57,156 --> 00:09:00,623
The amounts in different rows do not stack.

158
00:09:00,923 --> 00:09:04,367
Second, every qualifying policy contributes R80

159
00:09:04,167 --> 00:09:07,206
including the policies between milestones.

160
00:09:07,506 --> 00:09:08,385
And third

161
00:09:08,185 --> 00:09:12,735
the upper rows are arithmetic examples at those portfolio sizes.

162
00:09:12,535 --> 00:09:16,269
They don't mean that any one person will reach them

163
00:09:16,069 --> 00:09:18,784
or personally receive the whole pool.

164
00:09:19,084 --> 00:09:24,088
And throughout, the customer's package stays at R430 a month.

165
00:09:25,388 --> 00:09:28,001
So what does this look like in a real month?

166
00:09:28,301 --> 00:09:29,356
This month

167
00:09:29,156 --> 00:09:33,631
Thandi personally services 10 qualifying paid policies.

168
00:09:33,431 --> 00:09:35,963
Here is her example statement.

169
00:09:36,263 --> 00:09:41,960
10 times R430: R4, 300 in customer payments.

170
00:09:42,260 --> 00:09:43,597
10 times R80:

171
00:09:43,397 --> 00:09:47,794
R800 allocated to the monthly compensation pool.

172
00:09:48,094 --> 00:09:51,584
That leaves R3, 500 outside the allocation.

173
00:09:51,384 --> 00:09:56,022
How it is used depends on the actual product arrangements

174
00:09:55,822 --> 00:09:59,159
including the insurance behind the cover.

175
00:09:59,459 --> 00:10:03,571
Part of that amount has to fund the obligations behind the package

176
00:10:03,371 --> 00:10:05,848
so none of it should be read as profit.

177
00:10:06,148 --> 00:10:11,158
Thandi has passed the 8-policy milestone and is working towards 16.

178
00:10:10,958 --> 00:10:14,101
Her ninth and tenth policies still count.

179
00:10:14,401 --> 00:10:15,781
Now meet Sipho

180
00:10:15,581 --> 00:10:22,073
a separately appointed consultant who services 6 qualifying policies of his own.

181
00:10:21,873 --> 00:10:25,611
His portfolio generates its own pool of R480.

182
00:10:25,911 --> 00:10:28,669
Thandi introduced Sipho to the company

183
00:10:28,469 --> 00:10:32,014
but she receives no portfolio credit for his sales.

184
00:10:31,814 --> 00:10:36,998
Each consultant's figures come only from the families they personally serve.

185
00:10:37,298 --> 00:10:40,021
So Thandi's statement grows only one way:

186
00:10:39,821 --> 00:10:43,713
by looking after more families, and looking after them well.

187
00:10:44,013 --> 00:10:48,406
And through all of this, Ayanda still pays R430.

188
00:10:49,706 --> 00:10:53,219
A policy is a relationship, not a single sale.

189
00:10:53,019 --> 00:10:57,469
Here is what service looks like after the policy is issued.

190
00:10:57,769 --> 00:11:00,693
Thandi helps Ayanda find a document.

191
00:11:00,493 --> 00:11:03,340
She checks an administrative query.

192
00:11:03,140 --> 00:11:05,913
And when Ayanda asks about claims

193
00:11:05,713 --> 00:11:09,620
Thandi directs her to the correct claims contact.

194
00:11:09,920 --> 00:11:10,526
Later

195
00:11:10,326 --> 00:11:14,456
Ayanda sits down with her mother and shows her the folder:

196
00:11:14,256 --> 00:11:16,692
the schedule, the claims contact

197
00:11:16,492 --> 00:11:18,996
and the number saved in her phone.

198
00:11:19,296 --> 00:11:22,816
The question from the beginning now has an answer.

199
00:11:22,616 --> 00:11:24,742
The family knows who to call.

200
00:11:26,042 --> 00:11:30,788
Thandi's figures are calculated month by month.

201
00:11:30,588 --> 00:11:36,300
If 16 policies qualify in one month, the pool is R1, 280.

202
00:11:36,100 --> 00:11:40,555
If 15 qualify the next month, it is R1, 200.

203
00:11:40,855 --> 00:11:45,706
What a missed payment means for a family's cover is set by the policy terms.

204
00:11:45,506 --> 00:11:49,990
That is a separate question from the consultant's monthly calculation.

205
00:11:50,290 --> 00:11:52,590
If a policy is not paid in a month

206
00:11:52,390 --> 00:11:55,772
it simply does not contribute to the pool that month.

207
00:11:57,072 --> 00:11:59,662
So, what is the next step for you?

208
00:11:59,962 --> 00:12:03,845
If you're here for your family, visit myequigrowth.

209
00:12:03,645 --> 00:12:07,022
com or speak to an appointed representative.

210
00:12:06,822 --> 00:12:10,921
Review who is covered, the benefits, the policy terms

211
00:12:10,721 --> 00:12:12,149
and how to claim.

212
00:12:12,449 --> 00:12:15,638
If you're interested in becoming a consultant

213
00:12:15,438 --> 00:12:18,432
ask EquiGrowth for the appointment process

214
00:12:18,232 --> 00:12:20,316
the service responsibilities

215
00:12:20,116 --> 00:12:22,590
and the written remuneration terms.

216
00:12:22,890 --> 00:12:26,722
Whichever path you are on, ask for the details in writing

217
00:12:26,522 --> 00:12:28,475
and keep them in the folder.

218
00:12:28,775 --> 00:12:29,713
For Ayanda

219
00:12:29,513 --> 00:12:34,811
the important thing is knowing what her family has in place and who to call.

220
00:12:34,611 --> 00:12:38,298
For Thandi, it is knowing which families she serves

221
00:12:38,098 --> 00:12:40,042
what each policy requires

222
00:12:39,842 --> 00:12:42,926
and how her monthly figures are calculated.

223
00:12:43,226 --> 00:12:46,931
That is how the revised EquiGrowth model fits together:

224
00:12:46,731 --> 00:12:48,588
one funeral cover package

225
00:12:48,388 --> 00:12:52,666
supported by consultants who look after their own policyholders.

226
00:12:55,166 --> 00:12:56,250
EquiGrowth.

227
00:12:56,050 --> 00:12:58,984
Empowering your financial journey.
